{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38024 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2''-Acetylastragalin and the High-affinity choline transporter, mediated through multiple targets. This connection is supported by the fact that 2''-Acetylastragalin acts as a target of several compounds, including Quercitrin-7-olate, Armepavine, and romidepsin, all of which have been shown to target the High-affinity choline transporter. The shared interaction with CCRF-HSB-2, a cell line that expresses the choline transporter, further strengthens this link. The evidence indicates that 2''-Acetylastragalin may influence the choline transporter through its ability to modulate the activity of these downstream compounds. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a possible role in regulating choline transporter function, likely through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
